<title>USA: C.R. Bard Q4 shr $0.46 vs $0.40.</title>
<headline>C.R. Bard Q4 shr $0.46 vs $0.40.</headline>
<dateline>MURRAY HILL, N.J. 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>C. R. BARD, INC. AND  SUBSIDIARIES</p>
<p>			  (In thousands except per share amounts)</p>
<p>	    Quarter Ended December 31,   Year Ended December 31,</p>
<p>		     1996	1995		 1996    1995</p>
<p>Net sales	314,200     $291,000     $1,194,400  $1,137,800</p>
<p>Total costs and</p>
<p> expenses     276,300	260,000	1,091,700    1,014,300</p>
<p>Net income   $ 26,500     $ 22,800     $   92,500    $  86,800</p>
<p>Net income</p>
<p> per share $    .46     $    .40     $     1.62    $    1.53</p>
<p>Weighted average</p>
<p>shares outstanding			     57,090	 56,731</p>
<p>NOTE: Q4 1995 results included a one-time after tax charge of $3.6 million or $0.06 per share for costs associated with the merger with American Hydro-Surgical Instruments Inc.</p>
<p>1996 results include one-time after-tax charges of $0.23 per share for the IMPRA acquisition and the Davol plant closing, while 1995 results include one-time charges of $0.23 for two acquisitions made that year.</p>
